    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12531317/comment/13149630",
          "id": "13149630",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "The solution is to define another queue for the tasks considered as low priority, so that they don't fill the execution queue.\nThen, depending on the executor's load poll this queue for additional work items.\n\nThe secondary queue will only be used as needed, and the load is configurable via the system property \n\"org.apache.jackrabbit.core.JackrabbitThreadPool.maxLoadForLowPriorityTasks\"\nThis property is meant to be used as a percent. 0 means disabled / the default is 75.\n\nThere are some timing issues with the indexing tests on account of this new async text extraction. I've tried to fix all of them, but there may be more.\n\nI haven't touched yet on the tika extraction that happens in a different process. I think that will need some minor refactoring as well.\n\nAttaching proposed patch.\n\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stillalex",
            "name": "stillalex",
            "key": "alex.parvulescu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alex.parvulescu&avatarId=41133"
            },
            "displayName": "Alex Deparvu",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-14T14:07:23.646+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-14T14:07:23.646+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12531317/comment/13150424",
          "id": "13150424",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "In general looks good to me.\n\nI'm not sure the communication between the threads in JackrabbitThreadPool\nis 100% correct. E.g. the first statement in RetryLowPriorityTask.run()\nchecks if the queue is empty. To me it seems like this should never\nhappen, right?\n\nStyle:\nShould we rather keep the JackrabbitThreadPool package private and\nonly expose the marker as public interface? How about renaming\nthe LOW_PRIORITY_MARKER to LowPriorityTask and extend it from\nRunnable? That way a client wouldn't have to implement Runnable\nand the marker interface.\n\nMinor:\n The method waitForTextExtractionTasksToFinish() already does an\nindex flush at the end. Aren't the additional index flush calls\nin IndexingQueueTest now obsolete?\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2011-11-15T12:25:31.038+0000",
          "updated": "2011-11-15T12:25:31.038+0000"
        },
        {
